    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17611" textLabel="β-carotene isomerase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="C7AU21" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="944.2652587890625" centerY="648.077392578125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">The |FRAME: G-15330 DWARF27| gene of |FRAME: TAX-39947 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; Japonica Group| encodes a |FRAME: MONOMER-17611 &amp;beta;-carotene isomerase| that catalyzes the revesible isomerization of |FRAME: CPD1F-129 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene| and |FRAME: CPD-14646 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene| |CITS: [22422982]|. Earlier work has shown that |FRAME: G-15330 DWARF27| mutants do not produce 2&apos;-epi-5-deoxystrigol (a strigolactone found in root exudates of rice seedlings) and exhibit increased tillers and reduced plant height. It was also found that the protein localizes in chloroplasts and is expressed mainly in vascular cells of shoots and roots |CITS: [19470589]|. The cDNA of the |FRAME: G-15330 DWARF27| gene was generated by RT-PCR and expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; as a maltose-binding protein fusion protein, and the recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity. The purified protein was tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and shown to catalyze the isomerization reaction |CITS: [22422982]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-17611" />
